So my feeling is that this requires some non-trivial work and thus it is not going to be included in 3.1.4 and potentially even 3.2.0 beta1.

What about merging #22342 instead for now as a temporay fix and merging this one later?

@paulidale @mspncp ?

@mspncp thanks for the reeducation :)  I'd forgotten about the seeding APIs.  They are used for a DRBG to get seeding material and are not used or exposed by the EVP APIs.  FIPS convoluted things by mandating continuous tests and an external seed source.

The proper fix to the earlier issue would have been to use these as you've done here but being dense and forgetting about them led me to use the generate call instead.

I 100% prefer this to both my previous fix and to the alternative "weakness" fix.  This is done properly, the rest are kludges.

comments:
It turns out that it's pretty easy to simulate this sort of failure on Unix too:

``` diff
diff --git a/providers/implementations/rands/seeding/rand_unix.c b/providers/implementations/rands/seeding/rand_unix.c
index 9a936d800d..8fae3a0621 100644
--- a/providers/implementations/rands/seeding/rand_unix.c
+++ b/providers/implementations/rands/seeding/rand_unix.c
@@ -641,7 +641,7 @@ size_t ossl_pool_acquire_entropy(RAND_POOL *pool)
         /* Maximum allowed number of consecutive unsuccessful attempts */
         int attempts = 3;
 
-        bytes_needed = ossl_rand_pool_bytes_needed(pool, 1 /*entropy_factor*/);
+        bytes_needed = ossl_rand_pool_bytes_needed(pool, 2 /*entropy_factor*/);
         while (bytes_needed != 0 && attempts-- > 0) {
             buffer = ossl_rand_pool_add_begin(pool, bytes_needed);
             bytes = syscall_random(buffer, bytes_needed);
```

I'm going to guess that this means that the other vOS gatherer may fail this test as well, 'cause:

https://github.com/openssl/openssl/blob/636ee1d0b864f29a70573a4894958958e940c01e/providers/implementations/rands/seeding/rand_unix.c#L155

